    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 0 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Finish the deal with the largest pile of cards by being the first of the matching players to call the other player's animal (or noise) when their top cards match in rank.",
      "Turn-flow example: 1. **The Choice**: Each player announces their chosen animal at the start. 2. **Turning**: Starting left of the dealer, each player flips the top card of their face-down pile face-up onto a personal face-up pile. Cards should be flipped AWAY from the player so everyone sees them at once. 3. **The Match**: When any two players' top face-up cards match in rank (e.g., two 8s), the first of those two players to make the OTHER player's animal noise (or shout their animal name) wins the match. 4. **Winning Piles**: The winner of the match takes both face-up piles and places them face-down at the bottom of their draw pile. 5. **Snap Pot (Optional)**: If any non-matching player shouts first, or a player makes a false sound, their face-up pile goes into a center 'Snap Pot'. The first person to identify a match with the Pot wins it.",
